<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Turkey</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Turkey is a modern country occupying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>. Its territory has been home to many ancient and medieval states, and accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> note the Old Assyrian merchant colony at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanesh">Kanesh</a> in central Anatolia. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> note that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>'s empire at its height included portions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and Turkey before contracting rapidly after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/turkey.jpg" alt="Turkey" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Benbennick (original author) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Turkey.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
